 as 90 percent by tweaking the dose  redmond shannon explains we wanted a  vaccine for the world  not just for high income countries not  just some of the team behind the oxford  university  astrazeneca vaccine share their good  news with royalty  in the most pandemic way possible on  zoom  it's an amazing achievement isn't it it  really is this latest shot in the arm to  covert 19  is the fourth late stage trial with  encouraging results  russia's sputnik 5 is reported to be 92  percent effective in protecting people  from covet 19.  the pfizer bioentech vaccine is said to  be at least  90 percent effective modernist protects  up to  95 percent of people this latest vaccine  appears to be 62 effective with two full  doses  but as high as 90 percent when the first  shot is a half dose  averaging out at 70 percent that might  sound low but none of the people who got  the vaccine and still got coveted 19  were hospitalized and this vaccine has  two big selling points  it is considerably cheaper than pfizers  or modernist  and it doesn't need to be kept as cold  you don't need a freezer to store the  vaccine you can  distribute it in the conventional way  for all vaccines  keeping them in a two to eight degree  centigrade fridge  that is big news in countries that lack  special freezer facilities  the uk has 4 million doses ready to go  with regulatory approval possibly coming  as early as next month  the bulk of the vaccine rollout program  will be in  january february march and we hope  that sometime after easter  things will be able to start to get back  to normal the oxford vaccine makes up  20 million of canada's 358 million  covert 19 vaccine orders  we have built up a really robust  portfolio of orders and purchases  it's going to be essential to have close  collaboration between the federal  government  and the premiers of the provinces as the  second wave continues across canada and  here in europe  medical experts and politicians warn  against thinking the fi